# Frontend UI Rules

## Component Standards
- All glass surfaces use `<GlassCard>` — never a plain `<div>` with a background color or backdrop-filter.
- Shared primitives live in `src/components/ui/` — no duplicates in feature or page files.
- Layout chrome (nav, tab bar) lives in `src/components/layout/`.
- Feature widgets (SparkChart, PlatformLogo, WatchlistButton) live in `src/components/features/`.
- `src/components/ui/` must not import from `src/components/features/`.

## Data Loading
- Server Components fetch initial page data directly (trending lists, product metadata).
- Price data is always fetched client-side via SWR — prices change frequently and must not be cached at the SSR layer.
- SWR pattern for price routes:
  ```tsx
  const { data, isLoading } = useSWR(
    `/api/prices/${category}?q=${query}&city=${city}`,
    fetcher,
    { refreshInterval: 300_000 }
  )
  ```
- Every async Server Component that fetches data must be wrapped in a `<Suspense>` boundary with a skeleton component that matches the loaded layout.
- Skeletons must match the visual shape of the real content (same card height, same grid columns).

## Global State (Zustand)
- Three stores only: `useThemeStore` (theme), `useCityStore` (active city), `useAuthStore` (session).
- No per-component or per-feature state goes into Zustand stores.
- Watchlist and alert mutations use SWR optimistic updates — not Zustand.

## Accessibility
- Every interactive element has a visible `focus-visible` outline using `var(--accent)` or a token-derived ring.
- Minimum touch target size: 44×44px for all tappable controls.
- Semantic roles and labels are required on: tabs, toggles, dialogs, alerts, inputs, icon-only buttons.
- WCAG AA contrast enforced for all text and icon colors in both dark and light themes.
- All motion-capable components check `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` and skip animation if set.

## Responsive Layout
- Mobile-first default. Desktop enhancements applied at `lg` (1024px) and `xl` (1280px).
- Mobile content gutters: 16–20px. Desktop content gutters: 24–32px.
- **Desktop shell** (`≥ 1024px`): `DesktopNav` 220px fixed left + `<main>` flex-1, no TabBar.
- **Mobile shell** (`< 1024px`): no side nav, `TabBar` fixed bottom, `<main>` has `padding-bottom: 100px`.
- `DesktopNav` and `TabBar` are both `"use client"` components (active state requires client navigation hooks).

## Route Layer Discipline
- `app/**/page.tsx` files are composition only — no inline data fetching logic, no business logic.
- Sticky mobile CTAs and screen-specific chrome belong in the page file, not inside shared components.
- Dynamic segments (`[query]`, `[id]`) are validated in the route before being passed to components.

## Patterns to Follow
```tsx
// Page enter animation — apply to root div of every page
const pageVariants = {
  initial: { opacity: 0, y: 12 },
  animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0, transition: { duration: 0.22, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] } }
}

// List stagger — wrap list container and items
const container = { animate: { transition: { staggerChildren: 0.04 } } }
const item = { initial: { opacity: 0, y: 10 }, animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0, transition: { duration: 0.2 } } }

// Sort reorder — each card gets layout + layoutId
<motion.div layout layoutId={`card-${platform}`}>
```
